data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# d002 — implement and test greet()\\n\\n## What was delivered\\n\\nOn branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>` in `~/subject`, commit `cbec321`\\n(\\\"Add greet() function with unit tests\\\"):\\n\\n- `src/greet.py` — `greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py` — unittest `TestCase` with two tests:\\n  - `test_normal_name`: `greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`\\n  - `test_empty_string`: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n  - The test file inserts `../src` onto `sys.path` at import time so\\n    `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` can locate and import `greet`\\n    without a package/`__init__.py` or installed package.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nRan from the repo root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n```\\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit code 0, both tests passed.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Repo previously contained only `README.md`; `src/` and `tests/` directories\\n  were created fresh.\\n- No blockers encountered; scope matched the dispatch exactly.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

